course: dictionary
lesson: 1908
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning the writer wants. «Newspaper features include a headline, a photo, a caption and columns.» Here, columns are parts of a newspaper page, not stacks of things.
explain: «A tornado is a narrow spinning column of air that reaches from a thunderstorm cloud down to the ground.» Here, column means a tall, thin shape standing up, like a pillar. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A tall, thin shape of air fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: In a table, a column goes up and down, and a row goes across. Remember it like this: a column climbs, and a row rows across.
fact: Column means a line of things going straight up and down, one under another.
fact: In a table, a column runs up and down and a row runs across.
fact: A column can also be a tall stone post that holds up a roof, like the old Greek columns.
fact: In a newspaper, a column is a regular article, as in «Newspaper features include a headline, a photo, a caption and columns.»
fact: Context helps you choose the right meaning: «A tornado is a narrow spinning column of air» means a tall, thin shape, not a line of numbers.
exercise: «A tornado is a narrow spinning column of air.» In this sentence, what does column mean? | A line of people singing together | A way of cooking eggs | A word for a loud noise | *A tall, thin shape reaching from a cloud to the ground
exercise: In a table, which way does a column run? | Slantwise from corner to corner | *Up and down | Across the page | Round in circles
exercise: In a table, what does a row do? | Is a newspaper article | Runs up and down | Holds up a roof | *Runs across
test: «Newspaper features include a headline, a photo, a caption and columns.» Here, what is a column? | *A regular article in a newspaper | A line of ants marching | A drop of rain | A stone post in a Greek temple
test: Ayo has 4 columns of chairs, with 5 chairs in each column. How many chairs are there in total? | 9 | 15 | 45 | *20
exam: «Covering holes makes the shaking air column longer and the note lower.» What does column mean here? | A newspaper article | A line of people marching | *A tall line of air inside the pipe | A tall stone post
